1
00:00:01,235 --> 00:00:02,102
Ma'am!

2
00:00:02,169 --> 00:00:03,036
EPISODE 7

3
00:00:03,103 --> 00:00:04,438
Oh, hello there!

4
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:07,274
I told you to wait. Why are you here?

5
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:08,642
Who are you?

6
00:00:08,709 --> 00:00:12,112
Don't you remember me? It's Yoon.

7
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:14,982
The little kid who lived in Hadurok.

8
00:00:15,048 --> 00:00:17,317
The one who moved from Seoul as a kid…

9
00:00:17,384 --> 00:00:20,921
Yes! How long has it been?

10
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:23,590
You haven't changed a bit, ma'am.

11
00:00:25,259 --> 00:00:28,195
If you were coming home,
you could've let me say hi.

12
00:00:28,262 --> 00:00:31,231
Why'd you ditch me and run off alone?

13
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:35,569
Ma'am, I'm really thirsty.

14
00:00:35,636 --> 00:00:37,905
Could I get a glass of iced coffee?

15
00:00:38,572 --> 00:00:41,241
Sure, sure. Come in, come on in.

16
00:00:41,308 --> 00:00:42,509
Jeez.

17
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,979
-What are you doing? Let's go in.
-Gosh.

18
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:48,081
-Hurry! What's with you?
-Seriously.

19
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:50,050
What's wrong? Is this guy crazy?

20
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,972
Aw, how adorable!

21
00:01:12,606 --> 00:01:14,675
She's such a pretty little girl.

22
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:18,078
But how is she…

23
00:01:19,379 --> 00:01:22,883
She's Min-gi's sister.
I had her with his stepdad.

24
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:25,152
I see.

25
00:01:26,286 --> 00:01:30,023
-Then what about your husband…
-He cheated and walked out.

26
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:32,926
You know, that typical cliché story.

27
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:37,731
I tried to stop Mom,
saying fate gave her no luck with men.

28
00:01:37,798 --> 00:01:39,633
-But she did it anyway.
-Hey!

29
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,934
You say that to Mom?

30
00:01:41,001 --> 00:01:42,669
What did I say?

31
00:01:44,705 --> 00:01:45,839
Gosh, that…

32
00:01:45,906 --> 00:01:48,675
Where are you going?
I said, where are you going?

33
00:01:48,742 --> 00:01:50,277
You have a death wish…

34
00:01:52,579 --> 00:01:54,815
Please try to understand him, ma'am.

35
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:57,818
It's okay, I understand completely.

36
00:01:57,884 --> 00:02:02,122
I did so many terrible things to him.

37
00:02:02,189 --> 00:02:04,691
Even so, he has a kind heart.

38
00:02:04,758 --> 00:02:08,161
What good is a kind heart?
He's still so immature and childish.

39
00:02:20,941 --> 00:02:23,610
THE LATE YOON HYE-RIM

40
00:02:28,482 --> 00:02:30,951
Have you been well?

41
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:34,921
It's been too long, right? I'm sorry.

42
00:02:37,858 --> 00:02:39,426
Happy birthday.

43
00:02:40,927 --> 00:02:42,129
Mom.

44
00:02:47,868 --> 00:02:49,670
Still, Mom, I think these days,

45
00:02:49,736 --> 00:02:52,339
I'm growing closer to the villagers.

46
00:02:52,406 --> 00:02:54,741
And that makes me feel really good.

47
00:02:54,808 --> 00:02:58,178
Right, I have something to tell you.

48
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:03,517
I met a woman who's a lot like you.

49
00:03:04,584 --> 00:03:06,687
Even acting tough when she's a softie,

50
00:03:06,753 --> 00:03:08,889
she's the spitting image of you, Mom.

51
00:03:09,423 --> 00:03:12,726
Plus, she says
she loves your songs the most.

52
00:03:12,793 --> 00:03:15,495
She's your superfan. A total superfan.

53
00:03:22,102 --> 00:03:23,737
And…

54
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:30,677
she smells a lot like you.

55
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:39,352
So whenever I see her…

56
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,393
I think of you.

57
00:04:01,875 --> 00:04:03,443
Mom.

58
00:04:06,713 --> 00:04:08,882
I miss you.

59
00:04:19,793 --> 00:04:21,428
Want another iced coffee?

60
00:04:21,495 --> 00:04:25,232
No, thank you. I've already had four.

61
00:04:25,999 --> 00:04:29,536
How forgetful of me!
I should at least feed you a meal.

62
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:32,606
No, it's fine, ma'am. It's really fine.

63
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:37,310
Hey, where were you until now?

64
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:42,115
If it's broken, you should change it.

65
00:04:59,866 --> 00:05:01,535
Let's go.

66
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:11,912
I'm leaving.

67
00:05:15,115 --> 00:05:17,150
You could at least eat before you go.

68
00:05:17,217 --> 00:05:18,351
I said I'm fine.

69
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:20,120
Goodbye.

70
00:05:28,862 --> 00:05:31,731
-What are you doing right now?
-Half of this is mine.

71
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:41,374
Buy yourself something tasty.

72
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:44,277
Or buy Mom a new tracksuit.

73
00:05:46,546 --> 00:05:47,614
I'm heading out.

74
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:07,367
-What is this?
-Please tell me why you dislike me.

75
00:06:09,569 --> 00:06:13,373
My looks? My sense of humor? My wealth?

76
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:16,543
-I just dislike you.
-How can you just dislike me?

77
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:20,146
Until you give me
a reason that I can accept,

78
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:22,949
I will not move even a single step

79
00:06:23,016 --> 00:06:25,185
from this spot.

80
00:06:29,022 --> 00:06:32,092
Take that to the kitchen
and put it in the fridge.

81
00:06:32,158 --> 00:06:33,526
Yes, sir.

82
00:06:34,828 --> 00:06:37,297
Hey, we got spinach in yesterday.

83
00:06:37,364 --> 00:06:39,666
I'm only buying it
because it's you, okay?

84
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:42,369
Okay, stop rubbing it in, seriously.

85
00:06:42,435 --> 00:06:45,538
Hey, speaking of which, do me a favor.

86
00:06:45,605 --> 00:06:49,276
Our scheduled singer got stomach flu,
so now I have an open set.

87
00:06:49,342 --> 00:06:52,145
-Fill in for me, will you?
-Me?

88
00:06:52,212 --> 00:06:54,981
You want me to sing live like this?

89
00:06:55,048 --> 00:06:56,816
-Are you crazy?
-Don't want to?

90
00:06:56,883 --> 00:06:58,652
Then take the spinach back, punk.

91
00:06:58,718 --> 00:07:01,154
Seriously, that's so petty!

92
00:07:03,356 --> 00:07:04,691
Darn it.

93
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:40,794
Just in case you might

94
00:07:41,761 --> 00:07:44,898
Turn your head to look at me

95
00:07:44,965 --> 00:07:47,500
Even though it hurts

96
00:07:47,567 --> 00:07:50,036
I keep on smiling

97
00:07:50,103 --> 00:07:51,771
Here I am

98
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,942
My aching love

99
00:07:56,009 --> 00:08:00,613
Is always in the same place

100
00:08:10,623 --> 00:08:14,361
Min-gi, you actually sing pretty well.

101
00:08:14,427 --> 00:08:17,163
Did I or didn't I say I'm a singer?

102
00:08:18,264 --> 00:08:20,266
We sold all the spinach thanks to you.

103
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,202
Seriously, thank you.

104
00:08:24,104 --> 00:08:25,705
Oh, come on, seriously.

105
00:08:25,772 --> 00:08:27,507
Aren't you embarrassed by this?

106
00:08:27,574 --> 00:08:29,175
You're a woman. What is this?

107
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:31,711
Wearing that makes you stand out more.

108
00:08:31,778 --> 00:08:33,646
Why advertise, "I have money here"?

109
00:08:33,713 --> 00:08:36,683
Still, this right here is the safest.

110
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:40,487
There are always people
who let their guard down like that.

111
00:08:40,553 --> 00:08:42,989
Drop your guard like that,
and punks on bikes

112
00:08:43,056 --> 00:08:45,825
-will whoosh right by like this…
-Ow! Oh, no!

113
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:47,761
-Oh, no! Catch that guy!
-Yun-hui!

114
00:08:47,827 --> 00:08:49,963
Oh, no! My money, my money…

115
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:52,298
-Does money matter now?
-Money does matter!

116
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:54,200
Min-gi, what do I do about that?

117
00:08:54,267 --> 00:08:55,368
Ow, ouch…

118
00:08:55,435 --> 00:08:58,104
See! I told you not to be so stubborn.

119
00:08:58,171 --> 00:08:59,973
-Get up!
-What do I do now?

120
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,674
My money, my money, my money…

121
00:09:01,741 --> 00:09:04,077
Oh, Min-gi, my money, my money…

122
00:09:04,144 --> 00:09:05,445
Oh, ow!

123
00:09:05,512 --> 00:09:07,847
Oh, no, my money, my money!

124
00:09:07,914 --> 00:09:09,849
Hey, hurry and call the police!

125
00:09:09,916 --> 00:09:11,484
Just stop it already!

126
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:14,154
Stupid money, money, money!
Is it important now?

127
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,523
We should go to a hospital first, jeez.

128
00:09:38,445 --> 00:09:41,815
Ow, ouch… Oh, right!

129
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:46,419
Jeez, she's really too much.

130
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,822
Honestly, if it were me,

131
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:51,958
after all this effort,
I'd date me just out of pity.

132
00:09:53,326 --> 00:09:54,494
Darn it.

133
00:09:55,728 --> 00:09:57,163
Excuse me?

134
00:09:57,230 --> 00:09:58,798
Um, Su-yeon.

135
00:09:59,966 --> 00:10:01,067
Su-yeon?

136
00:10:01,968 --> 00:10:03,303
Su-yeon.

137
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:07,507
Su-yeon.

138
00:10:08,641 --> 00:10:11,711
Huh? Where did she go?

139
00:10:22,055 --> 00:10:25,291
Where did a woman go
in the dead of night with no fear?

140
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:26,793
Oh!

141
00:10:28,828 --> 00:10:31,698
What is that? What is that?

142
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:43,409
Su-yeon?

143
00:10:47,347 --> 00:10:49,782
What are you doing this late at night?

144
00:10:49,849 --> 00:10:52,485
Why are you shoveling
in someone else's field?

145
00:10:52,552 --> 00:10:55,288
Um, well…

146
00:10:55,355 --> 00:10:57,924
The thing is…

147
00:11:04,964 --> 00:11:06,599
Don't tell me you were just…

148
00:11:08,268 --> 00:11:09,869
stealing sweet potatoes?

149
00:11:11,137 --> 00:11:12,338
Yes, yes, yes.

150
00:11:14,374 --> 00:11:17,343
If you'd just asked,
they would've given you a few.

151
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:20,046
Why were you out stealing crops?

152
00:11:23,216 --> 00:11:24,951
It's thrilling, you know.

153
00:11:25,618 --> 00:11:28,655
And I love sweet potatoes so much.

154
00:11:35,161 --> 00:11:37,297
What is this?

155
00:11:41,434 --> 00:11:44,404
Aren't these night-vision goggles?

156
00:11:45,738 --> 00:11:47,907
Don't tell me you were afraid…

157
00:11:50,076 --> 00:11:52,412
a flashlight would give you away?

158
00:11:53,613 --> 00:11:56,783
What? Yes, yes, yes.

159
00:11:56,849 --> 00:11:59,319
Wow, you even steal systematically.

160
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:01,754
Even night-vision goggles, wow.

161
00:12:01,821 --> 00:12:03,323
Um, excuse me.

162
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:07,460
Could you keep this a secret…

163
00:12:09,195 --> 00:12:11,464
But I have one condition.

164
00:12:11,531 --> 00:12:14,500
Please tell me why you don't like me.

165
00:12:18,171 --> 00:12:20,340
Well, I mean…

166
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:22,642
it was all so sudden,

167
00:12:22,709 --> 00:12:24,711
and we barely know each other.

168
00:12:24,777 --> 00:12:27,347
I don't even know your name yet.

169
00:12:28,348 --> 00:12:32,652
So it's not because you dislike me?

170
00:12:32,719 --> 00:12:34,587
I wasn't totally rejected, right?

171
00:12:34,654 --> 00:12:36,222
Right? Am I right?

172
00:12:36,289 --> 00:12:39,759
What? Yes, well, I guess so?

173
00:12:40,793 --> 00:12:42,328
Um, so now,

174
00:12:42,395 --> 00:12:45,398
you'll keep this a secret, right?

175
00:12:45,465 --> 00:12:48,001
Don't worry about a thing.

176
00:12:48,067 --> 00:12:51,604
I am not one to go back on my word.

177
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:53,773
Thank you.

178
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:56,142
I'll get going then.

179
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,082
Su-yeon!

180
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,457
Yes?

181
00:13:13,259 --> 00:13:15,295
You should take your sweet potatoes.

182
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:24,070
Okay.

183
00:13:26,272 --> 00:13:29,709
A purse snatcher?
Is that why her leg is like this?

184
00:13:29,776 --> 00:13:30,777
What did they say?

185
00:13:30,843 --> 00:13:35,448
It's just a minor sprain.
They said a few days of rest will do.

186
00:13:35,515 --> 00:13:38,685
Jeez, she had to hurt her other foot.

187
00:13:38,751 --> 00:13:40,920
Now she can't use either foot.

188
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:43,056
Yun-hui, are you okay?

189
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:47,160
Oh, no, my money! My money, my money!

190
00:13:47,226 --> 00:13:49,162
Hey, hurry and call the cops!

191
00:13:49,228 --> 00:13:50,863
Just stop it already!

192
00:13:50,930 --> 00:13:53,466
That stupid money!
Is money what matters now?

193
00:13:53,533 --> 00:13:55,802
You need the hospital first, jeez.

194
00:13:58,838 --> 00:14:00,606
Yun-hui?

195
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:03,476
Hey, I'm so exhausted.

196
00:14:03,543 --> 00:14:05,578
I'm just going to sleep.

197
00:14:15,888 --> 00:14:18,324
Gosh, seriously.

198
00:14:18,391 --> 00:14:21,027
How can a woman
headbang better than me?

199
00:14:44,117 --> 00:14:45,718
-Oh, gosh!
-My stomach hurts.

200
00:14:45,785 --> 00:14:47,854
-What?
-I said my stomach hurts!

201
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:50,022
I think I drank too much iced coffee.

202
00:14:50,089 --> 00:14:52,091
Hey! Hey, stop!

203
00:14:52,158 --> 00:14:53,359
Oh, no! Stop!

204
00:14:53,426 --> 00:14:55,128
It's one thing after another.

205
00:14:55,194 --> 00:14:56,729
-Hey, hey!
-Hold on!

206
00:14:56,796 --> 00:14:57,864
It's coming out!

207
00:14:57,930 --> 00:15:00,299
Hey, hey! It's really coming out!

208
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:01,834
-It's coming out!
-I stopped!

209
00:15:07,974 --> 00:15:09,742
Come on, get out! Get out!

210
00:15:09,809 --> 00:15:12,011
-Wait, wait!
-Just hold on a bit longer.

211
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:20,753
Go on ahead without me.

212
00:15:22,121 --> 00:15:24,457
I'm finished now.

213
00:15:24,524 --> 00:15:28,261
What are you talking about?
The high ground is right in sight!

214
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:31,264
Hey, it's really leaking! Oh, Min-gi!

215
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:33,800
-Step aside. Get on my back.
-Oh, no!

216
00:15:34,467 --> 00:15:38,104
It's leaking out! What do I do?

217
00:15:38,171 --> 00:15:40,440
-Min-gi, hurry, hurry!
-Got it!

218
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:42,475
Find it fast!

219
00:15:42,542 --> 00:15:46,145
-Oh, gosh!
-If you poop, you die! You die!

220
00:15:46,212 --> 00:15:48,080
Hurry! Where is it? Hurry!

221
00:15:48,147 --> 00:15:49,949
What do we do? It's locked.

222
00:15:50,016 --> 00:15:52,952
Darn it! What do we do? What do we do…

223
00:15:53,019 --> 00:15:54,720
-Min-gi, I…
-Should I get a bag?

224
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:56,422
A bag, my ass!

225
00:15:57,089 --> 00:16:00,259
Min-gi, my sphincter has given out.

226
00:16:00,326 --> 00:16:02,295
No! Don't poop, don't you dare poop!

227
00:16:02,361 --> 00:16:03,963
Clench your butthole!

228
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:05,665
Poop and I'll kill you! No!

229
00:16:05,731 --> 00:16:07,366
-Min-gi.
-Huh?

230
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:20,646
Yu-na, what are you doing here?

231
00:16:22,048 --> 00:16:26,085
I live here. What about you?

232
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:29,155
Oh! Um…

233
00:16:29,222 --> 00:16:31,824
Well, what happened is, um…

234
00:16:31,891 --> 00:16:34,293
Excuse me, did you say you live here?

235
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,263
I'm so sorry when we've just met.

236
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:43,936
Could I possibly use your restroom?

237
00:16:56,249 --> 00:16:57,817
I'm sorry, Yu-na.

238
00:16:57,884 --> 00:17:00,820
No need to be sorry. It's fine.

239
00:17:04,056 --> 00:17:07,093
But why are you dressed like that?

240
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:11,430
Well, um, the thing is…

241
00:17:11,497 --> 00:17:14,066
We're farming in the country.
Cabbage farming.

242
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:15,868
Cabbage farming?

243
00:17:17,570 --> 00:17:20,640
-Why?
-To sell cabbages and release an album.

244
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:25,077
Oh, uh, I see.

245
00:17:33,686 --> 00:17:34,887
Darn it.

246
00:17:36,489 --> 00:17:38,958
So humiliating, seriously. Darn it.

247
00:17:39,025 --> 00:17:41,794
I drank too much iced coffee earlier.

248
00:17:44,297 --> 00:17:47,733
Still, I'm doing my business
in a celebrity's home.

249
00:17:48,467 --> 00:17:51,037
What an honor, truly an honor.

250
00:17:52,705 --> 00:17:54,373
Phew…

251
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:17,597
A celebrity's home sure is different.

252
00:18:18,297 --> 00:18:20,299
By the way, who's that woman?

253
00:18:20,833 --> 00:18:24,103
She's the Village Head
and Min-gi's first love.

254
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:28,541
-Hey, what are you talking about?
-First love?

255
00:18:30,176 --> 00:18:33,245
No, it's not like that.
As if she's my first love…

256
00:18:33,312 --> 00:18:37,350
She's just someone I want
to completely erase from my memory.

257
00:18:41,354 --> 00:18:43,522
Well, the feeling is mutual!

258
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:45,157
Are you satisfied now?

259
00:18:45,224 --> 00:18:46,659
If you're done, let's go.

260
00:18:46,726 --> 00:18:49,228
Why? Why don't you stay longer?

261
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:51,364
You missed her so much.

262
00:18:52,031 --> 00:18:54,700
-When did I ever?
-You did earlier.

263
00:18:54,767 --> 00:18:56,002
You scowled all day.

264
00:18:56,068 --> 00:18:58,738
-On and on about that woman--
-Lady, come out now!

265
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,339
Come out, come out!

266
00:19:04,043 --> 00:19:05,578
Gosh, seriously!

267
00:19:06,445 --> 00:19:09,081
Why put your dirty hand
over my mouth like that?

268
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,883
Why embarrass me like that?

269
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:13,653
Wow, you know how to feel embarrassed?

270
00:19:13,719 --> 00:19:16,155
Gosh, in front of the one you like,

271
00:19:16,222 --> 00:19:17,990
this guy's a whole different guy.

272
00:19:18,057 --> 00:19:19,558
Why? You like her that much?

273
00:19:19,625 --> 00:19:21,027
Stop it.

274
00:19:24,096 --> 00:19:26,198
Long time no see. How have you been?

275
00:19:26,265 --> 00:19:28,200
Okay, well…

276
00:19:28,834 --> 00:19:30,870
Wow, your place is nice.

277
00:19:32,972 --> 00:19:34,774
Your CEO must treat you well.

278
00:19:37,677 --> 00:19:40,880
Treat me well? Hardly.

279
00:19:40,946 --> 00:19:43,582
Um, about that thing from back then…

280
00:19:43,649 --> 00:19:46,152
Don't worry, I'll keep my promise.

281
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:52,658
This is so ridiculous.

282
00:19:52,725 --> 00:19:55,561
They don't even offer
a guest a glass of juice here.

283
00:19:55,628 --> 00:19:58,597
What are you talking about now?
I said let's go already.

284
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:01,067
I'm parched, that's why.

285
00:20:01,133 --> 00:20:03,302
Have a drink first. I'll go get some.

286
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:04,904
Huh? Oh…

287
00:20:07,406 --> 00:20:09,075
Darn it.

288
00:20:11,744 --> 00:20:13,379
Darn it.

289
00:20:19,351 --> 00:20:21,020
Gosh.

290
00:20:30,029 --> 00:20:32,331
This is so exciting! Yahoo!

291
00:20:36,402 --> 00:20:39,638
We're already at your place.

292
00:20:40,539 --> 00:20:43,776
Well then, have a good night.

293
00:20:43,843 --> 00:20:45,277
-All right, then.
-Yes.

294
00:20:46,345 --> 00:20:48,013
Su-yeon!

295
00:20:50,149 --> 00:20:51,984
-Yes?
-Um…

296
00:20:54,653 --> 00:20:58,157
It's Han-cheol. Yoo Han-cheol.

297
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:01,260
That's my name.

298
00:21:02,128 --> 00:21:03,796
Please go inside and sleep.

299
00:21:03,863 --> 00:21:05,531
And be sure to dream of me.

300
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:17,209
What kind of guy is that?

301
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:20,780
Ki-jun! Ki-jun!

302
00:21:23,249 --> 00:21:25,284
Ki-jun!

303
00:21:25,351 --> 00:21:27,353
Where did he go again?

304
00:21:27,419 --> 00:21:29,588
Then I have to sleep alone tonight.

305
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:35,094
Help me! Somebody help!

306
00:21:35,161 --> 00:21:37,129
Please… Someone help me.

307
00:21:38,063 --> 00:21:40,132
It is no use.

308
00:21:40,199 --> 00:21:43,969
People here all sleep after sundown.

309
00:21:44,737 --> 00:21:46,605
This is seriously driving me crazy.

310
00:21:46,672 --> 00:21:49,241
How long do we have to stay like this?

311
00:21:50,409 --> 00:21:53,712
Don't just lie there. Yell too, Bul-ja.

312
00:21:55,714 --> 00:21:57,149
It is Hwa-ran.

313
00:21:57,216 --> 00:21:59,251
-Song Hwa-ran.
-What?

314
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:02,121
My name is Song Hwa-ran, not Bul-ja.

315
00:22:02,188 --> 00:22:03,622
Why does that matter now?

316
00:22:03,689 --> 00:22:06,091
Just yell for help, Bul-ja!

317
00:22:10,062 --> 00:22:11,197
Okay, okay.

318
00:22:11,263 --> 00:22:13,866
Yell for help, Hwa-ran!

319
00:22:17,236 --> 00:22:20,706
Somebody save us!

320
00:22:26,979 --> 00:22:29,181
You look really tired.

321
00:22:29,248 --> 00:22:30,916
Still really busy these days?

322
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:32,785
Same as always.

323
00:22:32,852 --> 00:22:35,387
Ask your agency for some herbal tonic.

324
00:22:35,454 --> 00:22:37,156
Your face looks so worn out.

325
00:22:37,223 --> 00:22:40,526
Don't skip meals when you're busy.
Make sure you eat well.

326
00:22:40,593 --> 00:22:41,994
Okay?

327
00:22:42,061 --> 00:22:44,396
Yes, I will.

328
00:22:51,403 --> 00:22:53,672
We should get going.

329
00:22:53,739 --> 00:22:55,574
Oh, are you leaving already?

330
00:22:55,641 --> 00:22:58,577
Yes, tomorrow morning,
I need to feed the cows.

331
00:22:58,644 --> 00:23:00,579
I also have to clean up pig poop.

332
00:23:00,646 --> 00:23:02,615
Right, it's late. We should head out.

333
00:23:03,148 --> 00:23:04,984
Let's go, Yun-hui.

334
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:07,086
-Need some help?
-No, I'm good.

335
00:23:07,152 --> 00:23:08,520
Gosh…

336
00:23:09,188 --> 00:23:11,357
Look what time it is.

337
00:23:14,927 --> 00:23:16,595
Hello?

338
00:23:18,964 --> 00:23:21,000
I told you I'm not going.

339
00:23:23,502 --> 00:23:26,272
I'm tired, so let's talk tomorrow.

340
00:23:29,808 --> 00:23:31,543
What was that call about?

341
00:23:33,012 --> 00:23:34,980
It's nothing. Nothing at all.

342
00:23:44,957 --> 00:23:47,860
Take care, and drive safely.

343
00:23:47,927 --> 00:23:50,863
Okay. You're sure nothing's wrong?

344
00:23:51,630 --> 00:23:54,366
I told you, I'm fine. Bye.

345
00:23:54,433 --> 00:23:56,402
-You too, Hyeok.
-Okay.

346
00:23:56,468 --> 00:23:58,404
Goodbye to you too, Village Head.

347
00:24:02,841 --> 00:24:04,510
I'm off.

348
00:24:21,026 --> 00:24:23,495
That place is like a palace, isn't it?

349
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:26,398
Hey, what's with that girl Yu-na?

350
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:28,834
She looked so pretty on TV.

351
00:24:28,901 --> 00:24:31,503
She only looks good on TV, just on TV.

352
00:24:32,104 --> 00:24:34,239
I knew it. I just knew it.

353
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:39,745
Lee Min-gi, what's with you again?

354
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:43,382
I can't do this. You two go ahead.

355
00:24:44,550 --> 00:24:47,453
Hey, Lee Min-gi! Where are you going?

356
00:24:47,519 --> 00:24:49,621
If you just leave, what about us?

357
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:55,094
Give it up. When it comes to Yu-na,

358
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:57,296
he'll drop everything and run to her.

359
00:24:58,030 --> 00:24:59,398
Then who will drive?

360
00:25:00,299 --> 00:25:03,035
-You have me.
-You said you can't drive.

361
00:25:03,102 --> 00:25:05,304
You can teach me. I'll catch on fast.

362
00:25:05,371 --> 00:25:07,006
I'm smart. I'm a med student.

363
00:25:12,311 --> 00:25:16,448
-Min-gi.
-Want a beer? It's been a while.

364
00:25:27,092 --> 00:25:29,028
Hey! What are you doing?

365
00:25:29,094 --> 00:25:32,331
How can you drive slower than a bike?

366
00:25:33,132 --> 00:25:34,633
Hey! Can't you hear me?

367
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:37,503
Speed up!
The cars behind us are going crazy!

368
00:25:39,838 --> 00:25:41,407
-Hey!
-Yes?

369
00:25:41,473 --> 00:25:42,975
-Step on it!
-Okay.

370
00:25:49,581 --> 00:25:52,418
Are you okay? Are you really okay?

371
00:25:52,484 --> 00:25:54,386
Damn it! Hey!

372
00:25:55,054 --> 00:25:57,723
-What do you think you're doing?
-Oh, no.

373
00:25:57,790 --> 00:25:59,391
Are you crazy?

374
00:25:59,458 --> 00:26:00,926
What's with you people!

375
00:26:00,993 --> 00:26:03,095
Oh, no, what do we do about her?

376
00:26:05,464 --> 00:26:06,865
Are you crazy?

377
00:26:06,932 --> 00:26:09,568
Oh, I'm so sorry. Are you badly hurt?

378
00:26:09,635 --> 00:26:11,437
Talk about rotten luck…

379
00:26:11,503 --> 00:26:13,739
Yes, I am terribly sorry. Oh, dear.

380
00:26:17,042 --> 00:26:18,577
You, get out!

381
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:26,618
-Cheers.

382
00:26:41,834 --> 00:26:43,569
Here, your beer snack.

383
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:47,773
This brings back memories.

384
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:49,975
It's been so long.

385
00:26:51,243 --> 00:26:53,479
We were broke.
This was always our snack.

386
00:26:55,114 --> 00:26:57,916
We were grateful just to have this.

387
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:05,624
But it doesn't taste like it used to.

388
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,995
So why did you come back?

389
00:27:10,863 --> 00:27:12,631
Were you worried about me?

390
00:27:14,366 --> 00:27:17,636
Uh, no, I just…

391
00:27:17,703 --> 00:27:19,338
Don't play innocent.

392
00:27:21,273 --> 00:27:23,041
It's really strange, though.

393
00:27:23,775 --> 00:27:24,977
What is?

394
00:27:25,043 --> 00:27:29,448
How you always show up
whenever I'm having a hard time.

395
00:27:31,617 --> 00:27:33,685
-I do?
-Yes.

396
00:27:34,953 --> 00:27:36,588
You always have.

397
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:41,360
I think I'll quit being a trainee.

398
00:27:41,426 --> 00:27:43,295
Who said you could quit?

399
00:27:43,896 --> 00:27:46,198
You have to be a star, no matter what.

400
00:27:46,265 --> 00:27:47,266
Really?

401
00:27:47,332 --> 00:27:48,967
You know, I…

402
00:27:49,034 --> 00:27:50,202
Beckham…

403
00:27:50,269 --> 00:27:51,803
I mean, no.

404
00:27:51,870 --> 00:27:53,172
Kurt Cobain!

405
00:27:53,238 --> 00:27:56,608
I'll surpass Kurt Cobain
and be a world-famous rock star.

406
00:27:56,675 --> 00:28:01,213
And you have to surpass Beyoncé
and become a world-famous star.

407
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:03,048
No matter what.

408
00:28:03,115 --> 00:28:04,650
What are you talking about?

409
00:28:05,317 --> 00:28:09,288
If you quit,
I'll have no reason to become a star.

410
00:28:09,955 --> 00:28:13,258
So even if it's just for my sake,

411
00:28:13,325 --> 00:28:16,261
please drop all thoughts of quitting.

412
00:28:16,328 --> 00:28:18,530
Well, that's what I mean.

413
00:28:20,499 --> 00:28:23,468
I'm not confessing to you,
so don't get the wrong idea.

414
00:28:24,937 --> 00:28:26,872
Did I really say that?

415
00:28:30,309 --> 00:28:33,545
I didn't even know my place
and spouted all that nonsense.

416
00:28:33,612 --> 00:28:36,882
Hey, Mr. Kurt Cobain.

417
00:28:37,683 --> 00:28:39,918
Let's have a drink, okay?

418
00:28:43,055 --> 00:28:44,990
-Cheers.

419
00:28:52,931 --> 00:28:54,266
YUN-HUI

420
00:28:57,202 --> 00:28:58,870
Who is it?

421
00:28:58,937 --> 00:29:00,806
A call I don't need to take.

422
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:03,175
-Want this?
-Sure.

423
00:29:04,610 --> 00:29:07,613
You can't park here!
Please move your car right now.

424
00:29:07,679 --> 00:29:09,881
Wow, that punk turned off his phone.

425
00:29:09,948 --> 00:29:12,551
Wow, what a rotten jerk! Unbelievable.

426
00:29:12,618 --> 00:29:15,654
Gosh, what do I do about this now?

427
00:29:17,389 --> 00:29:20,292
I'm a crazy bitch
for letting you drive.

428
00:29:22,361 --> 00:29:24,930
-I'm sorry.
-Does saying sorry fix everything?

429
00:29:24,997 --> 00:29:26,064
I don't care!

430
00:29:26,131 --> 00:29:28,634
It's all your fault.
You take responsibility.

431
00:29:30,836 --> 00:29:33,538
Um, I do have one good idea…

432
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:35,440
What kind of idea?

433
00:29:38,043 --> 00:29:39,945
Man, as a designated driver,

434
00:29:40,012 --> 00:29:41,847
I've never driven over 400 km.

435
00:29:41,913 --> 00:29:43,548
By the way, sir.

436
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:46,551
Isn't a 250,000-won fare a bit much?

437
00:29:46,618 --> 00:29:48,186
Can't you lower it a little?

438
00:29:48,253 --> 00:29:50,188
I already told you, I can't.

439
00:29:50,255 --> 00:29:54,660
He's a fine, strapping guy,
so how can he not even drive?

440
00:29:55,327 --> 00:29:57,429
You picked the wrong husband.

441
00:29:58,030 --> 00:29:59,331
Husband?

442
00:29:59,398 --> 00:30:02,000
Oh, tell me about it.

443
00:30:02,067 --> 00:30:04,369
He can't drive, he can't make money.

444
00:30:04,436 --> 00:30:07,372
The man doesn't have
an ounce of competence in him.

445
00:30:07,439 --> 00:30:11,276
To add insult to injury,
I even hurt my leg.

446
00:30:11,343 --> 00:30:15,047
I have a baby in my belly,
and the weather's getting colder.

447
00:30:15,113 --> 00:30:19,718
My belly keeps getting bigger,
I have no money for the hospital, and…

448
00:30:20,686 --> 00:30:23,689
I'm just so sorry, my baby, so sorry.

449
00:30:25,324 --> 00:30:28,694
All right, I'll take 50,000 won off.

450
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:33,031
Really? Oh, thank you so much!

451
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:37,336
He's so kind to us, right, honey?

452
00:30:41,239 --> 00:30:43,008
The beer's…

453
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:45,177
here.

454
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:43,935
Here's 200,000 won. Count it.

455
00:31:44,002 --> 00:31:45,937
I'm sure it's all there.

456
00:31:46,004 --> 00:31:49,040
By the way, where's the bus stop?

457
00:31:49,107 --> 00:31:51,143
Head straight down this way,

458
00:31:51,209 --> 00:31:54,112
and you'll see it in about 20 minutes.

459
00:31:54,179 --> 00:31:58,483
But the first bus is still a ways off.

460
00:31:58,550 --> 00:32:00,118
I'll just have to wait.

461
00:32:00,185 --> 00:32:01,553
Goodbye, then.

462
00:32:01,620 --> 00:32:03,355
Yes, thanks for your trouble.

463
00:32:04,656 --> 00:32:06,591
Hey, you.

464
00:32:06,658 --> 00:32:08,894
Treat your wife better.

465
00:32:11,496 --> 00:32:13,732
We'll be happy together, mister.

466
00:32:13,799 --> 00:32:15,567
-We'll be happy together.
-Yes.

467
00:32:15,634 --> 00:32:17,602
What on earth are you talking about?

468
00:32:17,669 --> 00:32:21,406
What's this about a driver and a wife?

469
00:32:21,473 --> 00:32:22,874
I don't know!

470
00:32:22,941 --> 00:32:26,244
Because of this total pest,
I'm going crazy, just crazy!

471
00:33:01,613 --> 00:33:05,250
Stay right where you are.
I'll catch up to you soon.

472
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,452
Kurt Cobain

473
00:33:16,561 --> 00:33:18,630
Here, at least eat this.

474
00:33:21,166 --> 00:33:24,269
First nothing but ramen, and now corn?

475
00:33:24,336 --> 00:33:26,705
Who told you to tick off my aunt?

476
00:33:26,771 --> 00:33:28,707
Just be grateful and eat it.

477
00:33:32,143 --> 00:33:33,812
I'm exhausted.

478
00:33:35,447 --> 00:33:37,382
Hey, where did Ki-jun go?

479
00:33:37,449 --> 00:33:38,850
He didn't come home.

480
00:33:38,917 --> 00:33:42,053
-What? He stayed out all night?
-Yes.

481
00:33:42,120 --> 00:33:44,256
That punk Ki-jun won't even pick up.

482
00:33:44,322 --> 00:33:46,324
Where is that guy holed up?

483
00:33:46,391 --> 00:33:48,460
He's not a kid. What could happen?

484
00:33:48,527 --> 00:33:50,462
-He's a kid, a total kid.
-Really?

485
00:33:51,129 --> 00:33:53,832
Whatever. I'll get water. I'm thirsty.

486
00:33:53,899 --> 00:33:58,036
You startled me! My throat's dry too!

487
00:33:58,103 --> 00:34:00,605
-Don't you have hands?
-Why, you little…

488
00:34:01,439 --> 00:34:02,707
Sir.

489
00:34:04,142 --> 00:34:06,111
Please have some, dear brother.

490
00:34:06,177 --> 00:34:08,513
Sure, thanks.

491
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:16,655
That's so refreshing. Thanks.

492
00:34:16,721 --> 00:34:18,356
All gone.

493
00:34:18,423 --> 00:34:20,091
Thank you.

494
00:34:22,928 --> 00:34:25,163
Hey, so is Min-gi at Yu-na's place?

495
00:34:25,230 --> 00:34:27,332
So he stayed at Yu-na's all night?

496
00:34:27,966 --> 00:34:30,468
Won't that cause a scandal with Yu-na?

497
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:32,437
Do you mean the singer Yu-na?

498
00:34:32,504 --> 00:34:35,073
Yes, we were at Yu-na's yesterday.

499
00:34:35,140 --> 00:34:39,044
And I heard your sister
pooped right there yesterday!

500
00:34:39,110 --> 00:34:40,812
-That bastard…
-Unbelievable!

501
00:34:40,879 --> 00:34:43,381
How's Yu-na? Isn't she super pretty?

502
00:34:43,448 --> 00:34:48,353
Pfft, she's not even pretty.
It's all camera tricks and lighting.

503
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:51,957
I knew it! You can tell right away
she's just plain and bland.

504
00:34:52,023 --> 00:34:53,458
Plain?

505
00:34:53,525 --> 00:34:54,893
Bland?

506
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,628
Yu-na?

507
00:34:56,695 --> 00:35:00,465
Anyway, if another woman is
even a little prettier than them,

508
00:35:00,532 --> 00:35:03,134
they say they're all plain, every one.

509
00:35:03,201 --> 00:35:05,370
Please, I'm being totally objective.

510
00:35:05,437 --> 00:35:07,405
I just stated the objective facts.

511
00:35:07,472 --> 00:35:08,640
No way.

512
00:35:09,341 --> 00:35:11,009
Objective?

513
00:35:11,076 --> 00:35:13,678
Okay, then what about Lee Ha-nui?

514
00:35:13,745 --> 00:35:14,913
Lee Ha-nui?

515
00:35:16,047 --> 00:35:18,583
She just looks a little unique.

516
00:35:18,650 --> 00:35:21,720
-She doesn't have a pretty face.
-The former Miss Korea?

517
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:22,921
-Yes.
-The blowfish?

518
00:35:22,988 --> 00:35:25,490
Right, like a blowfish,
her chubby cheeks just…

519
00:35:25,557 --> 00:35:26,958
wobble like this.

520
00:35:27,025 --> 00:35:29,794
Come on, no way. That's ridiculous.

521
00:35:29,861 --> 00:35:31,863
Okay, then what about Han Hyo-joo?

522
00:35:31,930 --> 00:35:33,598
Han Hyo-joo's the prime example

523
00:35:33,665 --> 00:35:36,501
of a typical, ordinary face, right?

524
00:35:36,568 --> 00:35:38,470
She doesn't have a celebrity face.

525
00:35:38,536 --> 00:35:40,105
Right, with a face like that,

526
00:35:40,171 --> 00:35:42,273
my school has three or four per class.

527
00:35:44,776 --> 00:35:46,911
-Gosh, seriously!
-What? Come on.

528
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:49,447
That's absurd. Shame on you!

529
00:35:49,514 --> 00:35:51,049
Then go right now.

530
00:35:51,116 --> 00:35:52,784
You said three or four a class,

531
00:35:52,851 --> 00:35:54,819
so bring Lee Ha-nui and Han Hyo-joo.

532
00:35:54,886 --> 00:35:56,688
I'll pay a billion, 10 billion,

533
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:59,457
no, 100 trillion won, 100 trillion!

534
00:35:59,524 --> 00:36:01,026
Will you really pay me?

535
00:36:01,092 --> 00:36:03,361
Wait right here. I'll go get them now.

536
00:36:03,428 --> 00:36:05,497
No, no, forget it. Sit down, sit down.

537
00:36:05,563 --> 00:36:09,267
This problem won't be solved
even if the world ends, right?

538
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:10,435
Hey, Min-gi.

539
00:36:10,502 --> 00:36:12,804
You were with Yu-na? What did you do?

540
00:36:12,871 --> 00:36:14,372
Whatever. Let's talk later.

541
00:36:14,439 --> 00:36:16,474
I'm starving. Anything left for me?

542
00:36:17,809 --> 00:36:20,111
I warned you, no food if you're late.

543
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:22,781
Come on, don't be so petty again.

544
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:24,683
Petty?

545
00:36:25,617 --> 00:36:28,319
Know how much money
I wasted on your love games?

546
00:36:28,386 --> 00:36:32,057
I hired a designated driver
all the way from Seoul, a driver!

547
00:36:32,123 --> 00:36:33,925
-A designated driver?
-What for?

548
00:36:33,992 --> 00:36:36,027
Because of your precious friend, why?

549
00:36:36,094 --> 00:36:38,997
You guys are zero help in my life.

550
00:36:39,064 --> 00:36:42,400
You're all the bane of my existence.

551
00:36:44,235 --> 00:36:47,672
Come on, be honest.
What did you do with Yu-na all night?

552
00:36:47,739 --> 00:36:50,308
I told you, I drank beer.

553
00:36:50,375 --> 00:36:52,777
You only drank beer? Only beer?

554
00:36:52,844 --> 00:36:54,446
Nothing happened between us.

555
00:36:54,512 --> 00:36:57,015
-What are you thinking?
-Mind your own business.

556
00:36:57,082 --> 00:36:58,817
Have you boys seen Hwa-ran?

557
00:36:58,883 --> 00:37:00,885
Hwa-ran? I haven't seen her.

558
00:37:00,952 --> 00:37:03,655
She didn't come home all night.

559
00:37:03,722 --> 00:37:06,091
Where on earth did she go?

560
00:37:06,157 --> 00:37:09,227
Wait, Ki-jun didn't come home
last night either.

561
00:37:09,294 --> 00:37:12,697
Something smells fishy with those two.

562
00:37:17,102 --> 00:37:18,870
What is that?

563
00:37:20,004 --> 00:37:21,673
What's that?

564
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:25,210
-What are these two doing?
-They're real romantics.

565
00:37:25,276 --> 00:37:27,946
My goodness, what are they doing here?

566
00:37:28,012 --> 00:37:30,548
Why is it so noisy?

567
00:37:31,850 --> 00:37:33,585
Hey, guys.

568
00:37:37,655 --> 00:37:40,458
Whoa, no, guys!
It's not like that! Not like that!

569
00:37:40,525 --> 00:37:42,193
It's a total misunderstanding!

570
00:37:43,128 --> 00:37:46,364
Hwa-ran, wake up! Please wake up!

571
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:51,903
Oh, to be young! Must be nice!

572
00:37:57,575 --> 00:37:59,778
Where are you going?
It's not like that!

573
00:37:59,844 --> 00:38:02,180
Not again, not again!

574
00:38:02,847 --> 00:38:04,783
Guys, I'll explain. I'll explain!

575
00:38:04,849 --> 00:38:07,452
Move this first.
It's so heavy, it's killing me.

576
00:38:07,519 --> 00:38:08,820
Let's get them off him.

577
00:38:08,887 --> 00:38:12,123
Hurry, hurry!
This is seriously driving me crazy.

578
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:15,660
How did you even get under here?

579
00:38:15,727 --> 00:38:17,595
No, the bags fell on us!

580
00:38:17,662 --> 00:38:20,632
-Ugh!
-More this way, toward the front.

581
00:38:22,167 --> 00:38:24,102
Be careful, be careful.

582
00:38:28,106 --> 00:38:29,474
My legs are numb.

583
00:38:29,541 --> 00:38:32,510
Here's what happened. Yesterday, I--

584
00:38:32,577 --> 00:38:35,213
Hwa-ran, where are you going?
Don't go, explain!

585
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:37,048
Hey, hey, hey.

586
00:38:37,715 --> 00:38:41,186
You were caught red-handed.
What more is there to explain?

587
00:38:41,252 --> 00:38:44,255
It was an accident, an accident!
You saw us buried here!

588
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:47,458
What accident?
Look at the alibi you made up.

589
00:38:47,525 --> 00:38:49,861
You were together
all night with no excuse.

590
00:38:49,928 --> 00:38:51,329
"Lie under cabbage seeds?"

591
00:38:51,396 --> 00:38:53,097
What are you talking about?

592
00:38:53,164 --> 00:38:55,767
You think I'm that smart?
My IQ is two digits!

593
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:59,237
Whatever. I'm done caring about you.

594
00:38:59,938 --> 00:39:03,141
-Let's just go to work.
-I said it's really not like that!

595
00:39:03,708 --> 00:39:05,276
I'm losing my mind.

596
00:39:05,343 --> 00:39:08,346
-Why am I so jealous of him?
-I'm dying of jealousy too.

597
00:39:09,547 --> 00:39:11,015
Wow!

598
00:39:18,957 --> 00:39:20,358
It's a sprout.

599
00:39:21,159 --> 00:39:23,661
-Hey, they're sprouts!
-Look at these.

600
00:39:23,728 --> 00:39:26,264
-We really grew these, right?
-Yes, we did.

601
00:39:26,331 --> 00:39:28,700
Why am I so moved by this?

602
00:39:29,767 --> 00:39:32,036
Is this how a proud parent feels?

603
00:39:32,604 --> 00:39:34,606
Oh, our little babies are so cute.

604
00:39:34,672 --> 00:39:38,309
I mean, our seedlings are so pretty.

605
00:39:38,376 --> 00:39:39,911
Sprout One, Two, Three.

606
00:39:39,978 --> 00:39:42,046
-Are you naming all of them?
-Yes.

607
00:39:42,113 --> 00:39:44,382
-You crazy punk.
-Sprout Four, Sprout Five.

608
00:39:44,449 --> 00:39:48,286
You're putting on
a whole gift set of nonsense.

609
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:52,690
Come on, we're just touched.
It reminds us of how hard we worked.

610
00:39:52,757 --> 00:39:54,926
Your hard work isn't over yet.

611
00:39:54,993 --> 00:39:58,196
Cut the nonsense and get ready to work.

612
00:39:58,263 --> 00:40:00,331
Work? Wasn't it all done?

613
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:02,267
We just started. What do you mean?

614
00:40:02,333 --> 00:40:04,369
You water them morning and night.

615
00:40:04,435 --> 00:40:06,537
If it's hot, air out the greenhouse.

616
00:40:06,604 --> 00:40:09,874
Cover them if it's cold.
Once three or four true leaves grow,

617
00:40:09,941 --> 00:40:11,809
move them to the field, fertilize,

618
00:40:11,876 --> 00:40:13,945
and spray pesticide. It never ends.

619
00:40:14,812 --> 00:40:18,516
What are you doing?
They need water, so go grab the hose!

620
00:40:19,550 --> 00:40:23,788
Jeez, why is growing cabbages
more complicated than calculus?

621
00:40:27,225 --> 00:40:28,993
Such pretty little things.

622
00:40:29,060 --> 00:40:31,396
How can they be so green?

623
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:05,430
Good, they're just right.

624
00:41:07,031 --> 00:41:08,700
You can transplant them now.

625
00:41:08,766 --> 00:41:10,635
-Yes!

626
00:41:10,702 --> 00:41:12,804
But how do we do that?

627
00:41:12,870 --> 00:41:16,874
With an Italian artisan's touch,
you must plant each one by hand.

628
00:41:17,675 --> 00:41:19,811
-By hand?
-With our hands?

629
00:41:20,378 --> 00:41:24,382
It's the 21st century.
Isn't there a planting machine?

630
00:41:26,050 --> 00:41:28,820
Of course there is! How did you know?

631
00:41:29,587 --> 00:41:31,122
20 million won. Want one?

632
00:41:31,189 --> 00:41:33,291
-Wow.
-I'm sorry.

633
00:41:33,358 --> 00:41:35,426
Get moving! Take them to the field!

634
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:38,696
Plant them a generous 50 cm apart.

635
00:41:38,763 --> 00:41:43,267
Don't plant the cabbages too close,
or they'll overlap as they grow.

636
00:41:43,334 --> 00:41:46,738
Then they won't get enough sunlight,

637
00:41:46,804 --> 00:41:48,306
and with no room for airflow,

638
00:41:48,373 --> 00:41:51,909
they won't grow right
and will suffer from pests and blight.

639
00:41:51,976 --> 00:41:54,078
-Got that?
-Yes, Teacher.

640
00:41:57,048 --> 00:42:00,084
Let's take a quick break.
I'm too tired to keep going.

641
00:42:00,885 --> 00:42:03,688
Okay, let's take a quick break.

642
00:42:03,755 --> 00:42:05,923
Being hungry makes me even more tired.

643
00:42:05,990 --> 00:42:07,158
Are you boys hungry?

644
00:42:07,225 --> 00:42:09,594
-Yes!
-I'm starving to death!

645
00:42:09,660 --> 00:42:11,929
You punks. Follow me.

646
00:42:11,996 --> 00:42:14,499
I've got food so good it's to die for.

647
00:42:14,565 --> 00:42:17,468
I'll treat you to a special dish.

648
00:42:20,304 --> 00:42:21,439
Boss!

649
00:42:25,877 --> 00:42:27,879
Um, sir, is this what you meant

650
00:42:27,945 --> 00:42:31,249
by food so good it's to die for?

651
00:42:31,315 --> 00:42:32,750
You punks.

652
00:42:32,817 --> 00:42:35,586
Try them before you whine, you brats.

653
00:42:35,653 --> 00:42:36,954
Ugh, this smoke…

654
00:42:37,021 --> 00:42:39,057
This smoke really will kill us.

655
00:42:43,394 --> 00:42:46,464
All right, looks like they're done.

656
00:42:47,131 --> 00:42:49,734
What are you waiting for? Dig in!

657
00:42:51,436 --> 00:42:52,670
I'm not that tempted.

658
00:42:52,737 --> 00:42:55,740
Just trust me and give it a try.

659
00:42:59,944 --> 00:43:02,547
-What is this?
-Is this even edible?

660
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:09,754
The color looks good, though.

661
00:43:13,958 --> 00:43:15,927
Hey, awesome! What is this?

662
00:43:15,993 --> 00:43:17,528
-What is this?
-Why, why?

663
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:20,298
The beans taste like, uh, what is it?

664
00:43:20,364 --> 00:43:22,667
They taste like
straw-grilled pork belly!

665
00:43:22,733 --> 00:43:24,268
-Really?
-So they're good?

666
00:43:24,335 --> 00:43:25,570
This is incredible!

667
00:43:25,636 --> 00:43:28,372
I'll try. You guys have awful taste.

668
00:43:29,507 --> 00:43:31,075
Wow, this is really good!

669
00:43:32,143 --> 00:43:33,377
Unbelievable!

670
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:35,246
This is seriously delicious.

671
00:43:35,913 --> 00:43:36,981
Whoa!

672
00:43:37,048 --> 00:43:39,584
Wow, this is a real delicacy.

673
00:43:42,153 --> 00:43:44,288
Peel one open and two come out.

674
00:43:44,355 --> 00:43:48,192
Good, right?
That's what we call puffed beans,

675
00:43:48,259 --> 00:43:49,594
a country delicacy.

676
00:43:49,660 --> 00:43:52,930
Puffed beans? Wow, the name's weird.

677
00:43:52,997 --> 00:43:55,266
-But they're so good.
-Let's quit farming,

678
00:43:55,333 --> 00:43:57,068
sell puffed beans! They'd sell.

679
00:43:57,135 --> 00:44:00,037
Yes, let's do that!
Sir, please make more puffed beans.

680
00:44:00,104 --> 00:44:02,607
Stop stuffing your faces!
Aren't you working?

681
00:44:03,508 --> 00:44:06,144
Eun-u, please listen to me.

682
00:44:06,210 --> 00:44:08,946
I said no!
I'm not going to this crummy school!

683
00:44:09,013 --> 00:44:11,182
Stop being so stubborn. I'm exhausted.

684
00:44:11,249 --> 00:44:12,984
Then we can go back to Seoul.

685
00:44:13,050 --> 00:44:14,585
You know my business failed.

686
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:17,622
We have nowhere else to live…

687
00:44:19,056 --> 00:44:21,926
So just listen to me, please.

688
00:44:26,264 --> 00:44:28,399
I don't care! I hate you, Mom!

689
00:44:47,485 --> 00:44:49,387
Sang-deuk!

690
00:44:50,488 --> 00:44:53,024
Don't come over, don't come over!

691
00:44:53,090 --> 00:44:55,426
Why? What are you doing?

692
00:44:59,764 --> 00:45:01,732
I said don't come over here!

693
00:45:04,936 --> 00:45:08,005
Oh no, oh no! Don't come closer!

694
00:45:09,473 --> 00:45:10,808
Ugh!

695
00:45:16,681 --> 00:45:18,883
Oh my, oh my!

696
00:45:21,352 --> 00:45:23,688
I… I'm sorry.

697
00:45:33,231 --> 00:45:37,101
Um, I heard things didn't work out
with the woman from your blind date?

698
00:45:37,168 --> 00:45:38,803
You should've done better.

699
00:45:38,869 --> 00:45:41,405
That's none of your business.

700
00:45:42,273 --> 00:45:43,908
I'm sorry.

701
00:45:44,475 --> 00:45:47,044
This town sure has changed a lot.

702
00:45:48,212 --> 00:45:51,482
I wouldn't know. I see it every day.

703
00:45:53,284 --> 00:45:54,819
Oh, look, taro!

704
00:46:00,124 --> 00:46:02,159
Seeing this reminds me of back then.

705
00:46:03,694 --> 00:46:06,597
Remember that day in the rain shower?

706
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:12,903
Honey, how many kids should we have?

707
00:46:12,970 --> 00:46:16,540
Kids? Having just one
and living happily is plenty.

708
00:46:16,607 --> 00:46:18,943
Only one? No way.

709
00:46:19,010 --> 00:46:21,412
I'm going to have at least five!

710
00:46:21,479 --> 00:46:25,082
Maybe since I grew up lonely,
I love having a bustling family.

711
00:46:25,149 --> 00:46:27,752
Boy, still, isn't five a bit much?

712
00:46:27,818 --> 00:46:32,089
Your mom must've been lonely
living alone without your dad.

713
00:46:32,156 --> 00:46:35,159
And your grandpa
must've felt lonely outliving his son.

714
00:46:35,226 --> 00:46:38,596
So even if it's hard,
let's have five kids, okay?

715
00:46:40,031 --> 00:46:42,333
How can you be like this?

716
00:46:42,400 --> 00:46:43,401
Like what?

717
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:47,471
With a face that pretty,
how is your heart so kind too?

718
00:46:47,538 --> 00:46:49,440
Oh, stop it.

719
00:46:53,411 --> 00:46:55,980
Give me one good, deep kiss.

720
00:46:56,047 --> 00:46:57,948
What if someone sees us?

721
00:46:58,015 --> 00:46:59,917
Nobody's going to see us.

722
00:47:00,718 --> 00:47:02,553
No one's around here.

723
00:47:08,225 --> 00:47:11,228
-Wait, what's this?
-I think it's raining.

724
00:47:11,295 --> 00:47:13,531
My baby will catch a cold in the rain.

725
00:47:13,597 --> 00:47:14,965
Follow me.

726
00:47:21,972 --> 00:47:23,441
Stay right here.

727
00:47:47,565 --> 00:47:51,302
We were so happy back then, right?

728
00:47:51,369 --> 00:47:53,537
I don't remember. Not at all.

729
00:47:53,604 --> 00:47:56,607
Come on, you used this taro stem to…

730
00:47:56,674 --> 00:47:58,876
I told you I don't remember!

731
00:47:58,943 --> 00:48:01,979
Look, I don't remember
a thing that happened between us.

732
00:48:02,046 --> 00:48:03,848
I don't even want to remember.

733
00:48:03,914 --> 00:48:07,385
Even if I did remember,
I'd want to erase it all, got it?

734
00:48:07,451 --> 00:48:08,886
You show up after 17 years

735
00:48:08,953 --> 00:48:11,989
and keep acting
like nothing ever happened.

736
00:48:12,056 --> 00:48:14,125
I can't stand it anymore, so stop it.

737
00:48:16,727 --> 00:48:19,397
How I've lived all this time…

738
00:48:19,463 --> 00:48:21,265
do you have any idea at all?

739
00:48:24,869 --> 00:48:26,771
Oh my, this is bad!

740
00:48:26,837 --> 00:48:29,507
-Hey, hide, quick!
-Huh? Why?

741
00:48:29,573 --> 00:48:31,375
If my mom sees us like this,

742
00:48:31,442 --> 00:48:33,377
you and I are both dead!

743
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:39,350
Of course, ma'am.
Sang-deuk knows what he's doing.

744
00:48:39,417 --> 00:48:41,519
That girl, Mi-yeon or whatever,

745
00:48:41,585 --> 00:48:43,187
would he ever see her again?

746
00:48:43,254 --> 00:48:45,823
Unless he wants to see his mother die,

747
00:48:45,890 --> 00:48:47,391
he certainly won't.

748
00:48:47,458 --> 00:48:48,959
Absolutely, ma'am.

749
00:48:49,026 --> 00:48:52,296
Well, um, please go on ahead, okay?

750
00:48:52,363 --> 00:48:54,298
I have some urgent business, so…

751
00:48:54,365 --> 00:48:56,734
-Okay, I'll get going.
-Sure, don't worry.

752
00:48:56,801 --> 00:48:58,068
All right.

753
00:49:00,938 --> 00:49:03,240
Gosh, she's finally gone.

754
00:49:03,307 --> 00:49:04,608
I'm dying to pee!

755
00:49:04,675 --> 00:49:07,478
Why did that lady keep talking to me?

756
00:49:45,282 --> 00:49:48,118
Ugh, that's nasty, jeez.

757
00:49:56,093 --> 00:49:59,563
Oh no, what do I do?
My money, my money!

758
00:49:59,630 --> 00:50:02,533
No, my money! Oh no, my money!

759
00:50:02,600 --> 00:50:05,035
Hey, hurry and call the police!

760
00:50:05,102 --> 00:50:07,838
Knock it off! Does money matter now?

761
00:50:07,905 --> 00:50:09,874
Let's go to the hospital first, jeez.

762
00:50:12,476 --> 00:50:14,845
Why do I keep thinking about that?

763
00:50:14,912 --> 00:50:16,647
Am I out of my mind?

764
00:50:16,714 --> 00:50:18,649
Gosh, what am I doing…

765
00:50:20,618 --> 00:50:24,955
Still, I thought he was just a kid,

766
00:50:25,022 --> 00:50:27,391
but he actually feels like a real man.

767
00:50:29,460 --> 00:50:30,661
What are you doing?

768
00:50:33,264 --> 00:50:34,899
What are you doing?

769
00:50:35,900 --> 00:50:37,401
Oh, beans!

770
00:50:40,037 --> 00:50:42,439
-Can I have all these beans?
-Why the beans?

771
00:50:42,506 --> 00:50:45,209
To make puffed beans.
They're crazy good. So epic!

772
00:50:45,276 --> 00:50:48,379
No wonder your mouth is such a mess.

773
00:50:48,946 --> 00:50:50,047
Take them.

774
00:50:50,114 --> 00:50:52,316
Really? Thanks!

775
00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:55,419
Hey, this side's closer!

776
00:50:55,486 --> 00:50:57,888
Hey, hey! Those guys!

777
00:50:59,023 --> 00:51:00,624
Those damned jerks, really…

778
00:51:01,325 --> 00:51:03,427
Man, this… Wait, how long until it's…

779
00:51:03,494 --> 00:51:07,731
A real man, my foot…
He's just an immature kid, and I…

780
00:51:07,798 --> 00:51:11,769
I must've lost my mind for a second.

781
00:51:11,835 --> 00:51:14,738
Honey, come on, stop this and get up.

782
00:51:14,805 --> 00:51:17,708
You haven't eaten in days.
What are you trying to do?

783
00:51:17,775 --> 00:51:19,877
Forget it.

784
00:51:19,944 --> 00:51:24,448
A woman like me who can't cook
doesn't even deserve to eat.

785
00:51:24,515 --> 00:51:27,017
Please just leave me alone.

786
00:51:27,084 --> 00:51:30,120
Um, honey, come on.

787
00:51:32,389 --> 00:51:35,159
Man, she's so stubborn…

788
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:40,397
Goodness.

789
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:03,320
How on earth do these taste this good?

790
00:52:03,387 --> 00:52:04,788
We should just live here.

791
00:52:04,855 --> 00:52:06,423
Go on, eat up.

792
00:52:07,091 --> 00:52:09,126
Huh?

793
00:52:13,497 --> 00:52:16,934
Have you cooled off now, ma'am?

794
00:52:17,701 --> 00:52:18,702
No.

795
00:52:18,769 --> 00:52:21,372
Ma'am, those are really good, right?

796
00:52:22,573 --> 00:52:25,009
-No.
-Come on, you clearly like them.

797
00:52:25,075 --> 00:52:28,312
You're embarrassed, so look at you
keeping a poker face.

798
00:52:29,046 --> 00:52:30,114
Hey!

799
00:52:32,182 --> 00:52:34,551
Uh, sorry, ma'am.
I was just joking, sorry.

800
00:52:34,618 --> 00:52:37,287
Seriously, why did you provoke her…

801
00:52:46,797 --> 00:52:48,332
What was that?

802
00:52:48,399 --> 00:52:50,668
It was good, though. Ha, seriously.

803
00:52:54,605 --> 00:52:56,874
Eat plenty.

804
00:53:18,095 --> 00:53:19,930
Yun-hui, what are you doing?

805
00:53:20,497 --> 00:53:22,433
Can't you tell by looking?

806
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:28,338
Don't you smell herbal medicine?

807
00:53:28,405 --> 00:53:31,475
Yes, we feed this cow herbal medicine.

808
00:53:31,542 --> 00:53:33,610
It's Hanyaku, our town's specialty.

809
00:53:33,677 --> 00:53:35,979
Cows eat herbal medicine?
Even people can't?

810
00:53:36,046 --> 00:53:38,449
Wow, this cow is living the high life.

811
00:53:42,986 --> 00:53:44,354
Oh?

812
00:53:45,556 --> 00:53:47,991
What? What now? What's with you again?

813
00:53:48,058 --> 00:53:50,694
Where did you get that hairpin?

814
00:53:50,761 --> 00:53:52,129
Wow, whoever picked it

815
00:53:52,196 --> 00:53:55,199
chose well. Great taste. It's pretty.

816
00:53:55,265 --> 00:53:56,967
So it was you.

817
00:53:57,034 --> 00:54:00,938
No wonder it's so cheesy. Why?
A leftover gift for your girlfriend?

818
00:54:01,004 --> 00:54:03,273
No, I bought it just for you.

819
00:54:03,340 --> 00:54:04,641
Me?

820
00:54:05,309 --> 00:54:07,211
Why me?

821
00:54:08,378 --> 00:54:10,948
-Do you really not know?
-Of course I don't.

822
00:54:11,014 --> 00:54:13,817
That's why I'm asking.
Why would I ask if I knew?

823
00:54:14,485 --> 00:54:16,487
You really are a clueless woman.

824
00:54:22,059 --> 00:54:26,396
Why would a man give a woman a gift?

825
00:54:27,397 --> 00:54:30,400
-Do you really not know?
-Hey, what's with you?

826
00:54:33,504 --> 00:54:35,139
I…

827
00:54:36,039 --> 00:54:37,374
Yun-hee…

828
00:54:39,676 --> 00:54:41,111
I'm your husband.

829
00:54:41,178 --> 00:54:43,514
I can't make money,
but I make babies well.

830
00:54:43,580 --> 00:54:45,749
Jeez, you're messing with me again!

831
00:54:45,816 --> 00:54:48,318
Won't you go to bed before I hit you?

832
00:54:48,385 --> 00:54:50,254
I should sleep with my wife.

833
00:54:50,320 --> 00:54:53,757
Shall we try making
baby number five tonight, honey?

834
00:54:53,824 --> 00:54:57,895
Jeez! I let you off as cute,
and you just keep pushing it!

835
00:55:01,298 --> 00:55:04,802
-Let's go together, honey! Wait up!
-Forget it!

836
00:55:07,171 --> 00:55:11,141
Everything is a joke to that punk.

837
00:55:15,646 --> 00:55:19,750
Should I update my blog today?

838
00:55:21,785 --> 00:55:22,886
Gosh…

839
00:55:28,091 --> 00:55:29,593
WORLD PIANIST LEE HYEON-SEOK

840
00:55:31,762 --> 00:55:34,331
NAMED A TOP 10 MOST PROMISING MUSICIAN

841
00:55:37,234 --> 00:55:39,269
Give me money for school lunch.

842
00:55:41,772 --> 00:55:44,174
-What? Why so startled?
-What do you need?

843
00:55:44,241 --> 00:55:46,343
-What, school lunch money?
-Yes.

844
00:55:46,410 --> 00:55:48,645
Where did I put the money?

845
00:55:59,022 --> 00:56:00,624
Su-yeon.

846
00:56:09,600 --> 00:56:11,969
What are you doing here…

847
00:56:16,874 --> 00:56:20,911
I waited here just in case.

848
00:56:21,645 --> 00:56:23,780
Are you swiping sweet potatoes again?

849
00:56:24,548 --> 00:56:27,150
What? Oh, yes.

850
00:56:27,217 --> 00:56:30,153
I'll help you out tonight.

851
00:56:31,321 --> 00:56:34,024
-Pardon?
-Today, I thoroughly scouted out

852
00:56:34,091 --> 00:56:36,660
every sweet potato field in the area.

853
00:56:36,727 --> 00:56:38,896
Just trust me.

854
00:56:39,529 --> 00:56:41,064
Oh, right.

855
00:56:41,131 --> 00:56:44,134
What kind of sweet potatoes
do you like, Su-yeon?

856
00:56:44,201 --> 00:56:46,637
Pumpkin sweet potatoes, moist ones,

857
00:56:46,703 --> 00:56:49,439
or chestnut sweet potatoes?

858
00:56:51,308 --> 00:56:54,044
Oh, you like chestnut sweet potatoes.

859
00:57:08,325 --> 00:57:09,459
Wow.

860
00:57:10,360 --> 00:57:12,429
It's so big and beautiful.

861
00:57:12,496 --> 00:57:14,932
Su-yeon, isn't it big and beautiful?

862
00:57:14,998 --> 00:57:16,733
Oh, yes.

863
00:57:27,811 --> 00:57:31,315
It's mighty big and beautiful.

864
00:58:12,055 --> 00:58:13,090
VIPER

865
00:58:14,124 --> 00:58:17,094
I said to check in once a week.
Why haven't you called?

866
00:58:17,160 --> 00:58:18,962
You're making me miss you.

867
00:58:19,029 --> 00:58:20,731
Don't make your big bro mad.

868
00:58:20,797 --> 00:58:25,268
From your big bro Viper,
who's anxiously waiting for your call.

869
00:59:04,074 --> 00:59:06,910
Jeez, are you drinking again?

870
00:59:10,580 --> 00:59:12,416
Why? Did something happen again?

871
00:59:26,263 --> 00:59:29,066
-Pour me a glass too.
-You too?

872
00:59:31,902 --> 00:59:35,105
Why? Are you thinking about
that Yu-na or Yu-ja girl?

873
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:42,879
I'm only saying this
because I really care about you.

874
00:59:43,847 --> 00:59:45,549
Just give up now.

875
00:59:46,416 --> 00:59:48,718
I haven't lived all that long.

876
00:59:48,785 --> 00:59:51,888
But in life, getting your hopes up

877
00:59:51,955 --> 00:59:55,492
doesn't make the impossible happen.

878
00:59:59,229 --> 01:00:00,864
It doesn't matter

879
01:00:02,666 --> 01:00:05,936
whether she looks my way or not.

880
01:00:09,072 --> 01:00:12,609
She's in a much more glamorous
and higher place than I am.

881
01:00:14,678 --> 01:00:16,947
But to me, Yu-na has always been

882
01:00:18,081 --> 01:00:22,219
someone my heart aches and hurts for,

883
01:00:24,921 --> 01:00:27,657
and someone I want to protect.

884
01:00:28,959 --> 01:00:31,328
I don't know if I can do it forever,

885
01:00:31,394 --> 01:00:34,731
but if I can, I want to protect her.

886
01:00:38,435 --> 01:00:40,871
Once a real man makes up his mind,

887
01:00:40,937 --> 01:00:43,773
he has to cover the full warranty too.

888
01:00:55,619 --> 01:00:58,155
-Gosh, you scared me!
-Get that thing! Hurry!

889
01:00:58,221 --> 01:01:00,991
Gosh, what a fuss over a grasshopper.

890
01:01:01,057 --> 01:01:02,659
A grown man, over a tiny bug?

891
01:01:02,726 --> 01:01:04,995
Can you protect your woman like this?

892
01:01:05,061 --> 01:01:07,197
Is Yu-na the same as a grasshopper?

893
01:01:07,264 --> 01:01:08,965
Hurry, hurry! Get rid of that!

894
01:01:09,032 --> 01:01:11,034
Jeez, seriously, let go of me.

895
01:01:11,101 --> 01:01:14,037
Gosh, you're number one
in the world at making a fuss.

896
01:01:15,739 --> 01:01:17,841
How is this tiny grasshopper so scary?

897
01:01:17,908 --> 01:01:20,043
Look at you making such a huge fuss.

898
01:01:20,110 --> 01:01:21,211
It looks gross.

899
01:01:21,278 --> 01:01:23,046
-Tried fried grasshoppers?
-What?

900
01:01:23,113 --> 01:01:24,814
Oh? They're so nutty and tasty!

901
01:01:24,881 --> 01:01:27,384
What's this? Are you having an affair?

902
01:01:27,450 --> 01:01:29,653
That hurts your husband's feelings.

903
01:01:29,719 --> 01:01:32,956
Hey, didn't I tell you to knock it off?

904
01:01:33,557 --> 01:01:37,360
-Husband? What does that mean?
-It's a long story.

905
01:01:37,427 --> 01:01:40,263
He looks fine on the outside, I swear.

906
01:01:40,330 --> 01:01:43,400
-Everything's a joke to him.
-Could I have a drink too?

907
01:01:45,302 --> 01:01:47,437
-You too?
-Yes.

908
01:01:48,939 --> 01:01:51,841
All right, I'm in a lousy mood anyway.

909
01:01:51,908 --> 01:01:54,444
-Let's drink the night away!
-There's my glass.

910
01:01:56,246 --> 01:01:59,282
-You too. Let me pour you a glass.
-Okay.

911
01:02:00,150 --> 01:02:02,319
Both hands coming right in, I love it.

912
01:02:02,385 --> 01:02:04,287
Hey, we have to toast first!

913
01:02:04,354 --> 01:02:05,789
-Cheers!

914
01:02:11,228 --> 01:02:13,663
I can't tell if it's sweet or bitter.

915
01:02:14,698 --> 01:02:16,466
There are so many stars.

916
01:02:16,533 --> 01:02:18,735
I never knew there could be this many.

917
01:02:18,802 --> 01:02:20,770
So pretty.

918
01:02:26,476 --> 01:02:28,144
Really pretty.

919
01:02:29,079 --> 01:02:30,747
So pretty.
